# Vector indexes, full-text, and change feeds

Verified against `runtime/surrealdb/memory.surql` on SurrealDB 2.3.7.

## Vector (semantic) search
- Store embeddings as `array<float>`.
- Define an MTREE index sized to your embedder:
  `DEFINE INDEX semantic_vec ON semantic_memory FIELDS embedding MTREE DIMENSION 384 DIST COSINE;`
- K-nearest-neighbour query with the knn operator:
  `SELECT id, content FROM semantic_memory WHERE embedding <|5,COSINE|> $q;`
- Or score with a vector function:
  `SELECT content, vector::similarity::cosine(embedding, $q) AS score FROM semantic_memory ORDER BY score DESC;`
- Keep `DIMENSION` consistent with the model that produced `$q`.

## Full-text search
- Define an analyzer, then a SEARCH index:
  ```
  DEFINE ANALYZER doc TOKENIZERS blank,class FILTERS lowercase,ascii;
  DEFINE INDEX semantic_text ON semantic_memory FIELDS content SEARCH ANALYZER doc BM25 HIGHLIGHTS;
  ```
- Match with the `@@` operator; use a reference number to score/highlight:
  `SELECT content, search::score(1) AS score FROM semantic_memory WHERE content @1@ 'restore cluster' ORDER BY score DESC;`

## Change feeds (episodic / time-travel)
- `DEFINE TABLE episodic_memory SCHEMAFULL CHANGEFEED 30d;`
- Read historical versions with `VERSION` or inspect changes with `SHOW CHANGES FOR TABLE ...`.

## Hybrid retrieval
- SurrealQL lets you combine graph traversal, vector similarity, and filters in
  one statement — prefer a single round trip over stitching multiple queries.
